WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.900
In the vertebrate nervous system, neurons are separate cells.

2
00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:08.880
Each has its own membrane.

3
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:14.280
They pass signals across specialized contacts, rather than forming one fused net.

4
00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:16.340
That is the neuron doctrine.

5
00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:20.520
It matters because development has to wire cells together.

6
00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:24.800
And we can trace the direction of signal flow from cell to cell.

7
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.080
Two fine nerve branches meet.

8
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.660
Their contact connects separate cells.

9
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.900
Development gave evidence for this view.

10
00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:38.080
Wilhelm His argued that each nerve fibre grows out from a single young cell, a

11
00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:43.400
neuroblast. Cajal described growth cones at the tips of young axons in chick

12
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:47.740
embryos. He read them as advancing ends of growing fibres.

13
00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:50.560
Cajal's specimens were fixed and dead.

14
00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.480
Movement was an inference from still shapes.

15
00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:58.210
Separate cells also have a usual direction of signal flow.

16
00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:03.050
Signals enter through dendrites and the cell body, and leave through the axon.

17
00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.230
This is dynamic polarization.

18
00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:09.030
It helps explain one-way signalling through a chain of cells.

19
00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:14.510
It is a useful generalization, with exceptions, including synapses between

20
00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:15.510
dendrites.

21
00:01:16.083 --> 00:01:18.683
How could anyone follow a cell in crowded tissue?

22
00:01:19.763 --> 00:01:23.643
Golgi's black reaction fills a few neurons completely, while most stay pale.

23
00:01:24.503 --> 00:01:28.723
A single cell and its branches stand out, though branches leaving the section are

24
00:01:28.723 --> 00:01:33.343
cut off. Golgi read fine axon branches as a continuous net.

25
00:01:34.323 --> 00:01:37.723
Cajal found branches ending near other cells without joining them.

26
00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:41.327
The light microscope could not settle the disagreement.

27
00:01:42.447 --> 00:01:46.327
Fine branches touching, or passing close at different depths in a thick section,

28
00:01:46.327 --> 00:01:47.467
could look the same.

29
00:01:48.347 --> 00:01:50.447
The image could not tell contact from fusion.

30
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.200
The direct test came in the 1950s.

31
00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:60.000
Electron microscopy showed two separate membranes at chemical synapses, with a

32
00:01:60.000 --> 00:02:03.120
narrow cleft between them and small vesicles in the terminal.

33
00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:05.460
The gap was visible at last.

34
00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:09.000
Separate cells form circuits through specialized contacts.

35
00:02:10.033 --> 00:02:15.253
A smaller point: electrical synapses couple some neurons through channels that pass

36
00:02:15.253 --> 00:02:16.793
ions and small molecules.

37
00:02:17.773 --> 00:02:18.813
The channels can close.

38
00:02:19.773 --> 00:02:21.613
Each neuron still keeps its own membrane.
